<item><title>Kenyan farmers dig trenches to guard soil before El Niño rains</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenyan-farmers-dig-trenches-to-guard-soil-before-el-nino-fce911/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenyan-farmers-dig-trenches-to-guard-soil-before-el-nino-fce911/</guid><category>Kenya</category><description>Farmers in central Kenya are preparing for heavier-than-usual rains linked to El Niño, after floods washed away fertile topsoil on their farms.</description><pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 17:03:12 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenyan-farmers-dig-trenches-to-guard-soil-before-el-nino-fce911/share.jpg" length="42051" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/ke/kenyan-farmers-dig-trenches-to-guard-soil-before-el-nino-fce911/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
